    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0467" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2694</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Irkutsk</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d459-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Irkutsk</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic">September 12,
                        1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 14,
                            12.54 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. Czechs and Russian army compelled to evacuate Kazan during night of 9th.
                    Evacuation orderly; most valuable war material, including all good, removed
                    previously. French Military Mission left Kazan 6th for Simbirsk.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harris</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d459-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d459-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Legation in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
